From: Try Omarchy contributors
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: leave chosen shortcuts with macOS

Applies after the Try Omarchy guest-layout patch.

The host-keys patch hands the Mac's dedicated keys back to macOS, whatever
modifiers are held. Shortcuts such as Control-Right Arrow, which moves to
the next Space, use ordinary keys the guest needs, so full grab still
swallows them.

Let host-keys entries carry modifiers, as in 124+ctrl. Such an entry stays
with macOS only while exactly those modifiers are held. Its repeats and key
up follow its key down, so releasing Control before the arrow can't leave
the arrow held in the guest. Bare keycodes keep their meaning.

The capture swallows Command's flagsChanged, so a key pressed with Command
can reach the tap without the Command flag. Remember Command from its own
events so Command shortcuts still match, and put the flag back on the
shortcut handed to macOS.

diff --git a/qapi/ui.json b/qapi/ui.json
index d5a01cb..04fecbb 100644
--- a/qapi/ui.json
+++ b/qapi/ui.json
@@ -1446,7 +1446,10 @@
